data: {"id":"chatcmpl-01da08e8-1ab6-4371-ad44-742764e18821","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795549634,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Performance limits are crucial: handling hundreds of thousands of transactions within strict memory and time bounds requires careful optimization. The constraint that one transaction can remain open while many others begin/commit dictates against copying the 200,000-key state on every transaction BEGIN. Considering there's a limit of four open transactions, copying the entire state for each BEGIN is unnecessary and inefficient.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-01da08e8-1ab6-4371-ad44-742764e18821","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795549634,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"The initial calculation highlights the extreme operation count, leading to potential out-of-memory or time limit errors, especially considering the read/range records per transaction. Iterating through keys within range records on every range record isn't feasible, and the range count must be logarithmic to avoid performance issues. Addressing conflict detection (R22) is critical, particularly with a high volume of transactions and read/range operations. The focus is now on optimizing snapshot management (BEGIN, PUT/DELETE, READ, RANGE) and conflict detection for performance.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

data: {"id":"chatcmpl-01da08e8-1ab6-4371-ad44-742764e18821","object":"chat.completion.chunk","created":1795549634,"model":"gemini-4-carbon","choices":[{"index":0,"delta":{"reasoning_content":"BEGIN is $O(1)$ and PUT/DELETE/RANGE is $O(\\log M)$, where M is the max number of keys. Each update creates new nodes on the path from root to the updated node, making the modification efficient. At most, MAX_OPEN_TXNS = 4 transactions can run concurrently. A transaction's snapshot is simply its root pointer.\n\nThe transaction's state is stored efficiently. Snapshotting at BEGIN is a constant time operation, utilizing a persistent balanced search tree with path copying. PUT/DELETE/RANGE operations have logarithmic complexity concerning the number of keys. Concurrency constraints are handled by the MAX_OPEN_TXNS limit.\n\n\n"},"finish_reason":null}],"usage":null}

